separate map parser from the actual engine
map parser creates binary representation of the level geometry and creates the texture atlas
engine reads the binaries and creates the level

load each png file using stb
sort the images in descending order by the img width
allocate new memory block needed for the whole texture atlas
copy the image data to the newly allocated memory
store the data to the same binary where the level geometry is

binary need to have all the required entity information embedded (position of objects etc)

create one big VBO for the whole map -> only 1 draw call needed
use subimage property to access the needed part of the texture -> bind only 1 texture

example:
images, data not necessarily in sequential order
xxxxx  zzz  yyyyy  cc
xxxxx  zzz  yyyyy  cc
xxxxx       yyyyy

images organized:
xxxxx
xxxxx
xxxxx
yyyyy
yyyyy
yyyyy
zzz
zzz
cc
cc
->
xxxxx xxxxx xxxxx yyyyy yyyyy yyyyy zzz zzz cc cc

frustum culling